Theorem 1. Every continuous map of the disc to itself has a fixed point.

Suppose 1, the rank of H^1 of the circle.
R^1 observe.

Assume for contradiction that f moves every point.
Then the ray from f(x) through x meets the boundary,
and this gives a retraction of the disc onto its boundary circle.
Suppose 1, the rank of H^1 of the circle.
Suppose 0, the rank of H^1 of the disc.
Restrict.
Contradiction.

Hence f has a fixed point.
R^1 publish.
QED.
